3. Protect your ability to dual-license

This is the most important part of the strategy.

Keep ownership of your own code. Make sure you have the rights to offer it under both licenses.

Use a Contributor License Agreement (CLA). If you accept outside contributions, a CLA should explicitly grant the rights needed for commercial relicensing. Contributors can retain copyright, depending on the agreement. 
